    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "If the points $(2,a)$, $(-1,b)$ and $(c,-6)$ lie on the line with equation $y=-\\frac34x$, find the values of $a$, $b$ and $c$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=-\\frac32,\\quad b=\\frac34,\\quad c=8$.",
      "worked": "For $(2,a)$, $a=-\\frac34(2)=-\\frac32$. For $(-1,b)$, $b=-\\frac34(-1)=\\frac34$. For $(c,-6)$, solve $-6=-\\frac34c$, giving $c=(-6)(-\\frac43)=8$.",
